<title>HONG KONG: M.C.Packaging sells US$9mln venture stake.</title>
<headline>M.C.Packaging sells US$9mln venture stake.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>M.C. Packaging (Hong Kong) Ltd said it has agreed to sell a 26 percent interest of its metal plate printing joint venture Hangzhou M.C. Packaging Co Ltd in China to Top Glory (London) Ltd for US$8.95 million.</p>
<p>Hangzhou M.C. Packaging makes metal containers, and provides metal plate-printing and coating services from its production lines in Hangzhou in China. The venture is 51 percent owned by M.C. Packaging and 27 percent by Top Glory prior to the deal.</p>
<p>M.C. Packaging, which makes two-piece aluminium cans, tin containers and plastic bottles, said proceeds from the stake sale would be used as additional working capital.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
